Composing #472 (strided-rectangle record) with #474 (owned per-tile recon)
=========================================================================

Branch      perf/compose-rect-tileown, base main @ ee07b00
Host        Apple M4 Pro, 12 cores, macOS 26.5.2, aarch64
Build       cargo build --release, default features (+ tile-owned-recon where noted)
            no -C target-cpu=native; no `nice` on any timed run
Vectors     ~/tmp/rav1d-perf/vec/v4k_8tile.avif        3840x2160 4:4:4 8bpc,  4x2 tiles
            ~/tmp/rav1d-perf/vec/v4k_8tile_10b.avif    same, 10bpc
Reference   dav1d 1.5.4 --framedelay 1, measured in the SAME interleaved sweep
Method      two-point wall fit: each cell timed at 2 and at 20 frames,
            beta = (ms20 - ms2) / 18, so process startup drops out.
            Rotating arm order inside every cell; strict idle gate
            (a cell is DISCARDED and re-run if any foreign process exceeds
            25% CPU during it). Box polled to a full 60 s idle window before
            each sweep started.

ARMS
  base      main @ ee07b00
  rect      main + #472 (fix/rect-rowview, carrying #469 + #470)
  tko       main + #474 (perf/tile-owned-recon), RAV1D_TILE_OWNED=1
  both      this branch, RAV1D_TILE_OWNED=1
  bothoff   this branch, RAV1D_TILE_OWNED=0  -- same BINARY as `both`, so the
            both-vs-bothoff delta cannot be a codegen artifact
  dav1d_fd1 dav1d 1.5.4 --framedelay 1

