LIVENESS -- one arm was measuring nothing, and the counter caught it
  The first sweep's `both` arm at 10bpc DECLINED: the memory ceiling this
  branch adds (default 256 MB) rejects 8 tiles x ~50 MB of 10-bit planes, so
  the arm silently ran the shared-picture path. Proof, registrations/frame at
  t=8: with the default ceiling 10,852,772 -- byte-identical to `rect`'s count;
  with RAV1D_TILE_OWNED_MAX_MB=1024, 10,904,612. The 10bpc cells were re-run
  with the ceiling raised. The 8bpc arm was always live (200.5 MB < 256 MB),
  confirmed both by its registration count and by its +201.5 MB RSS.

NOT MEASURED
  x86_64 (do not extrapolate -- the loop-filter compact path that panics on
  macos-15-intel is `#[cfg(target_arch = "x86_64")]` and does not exist here);
  t=16 and t=12/24 oversubscription; any vector below 4K in the timed grid;
  any vector with loop restoration live (unchanged campaign-wide blindness --
  LR is off in both 4K gap vectors and active in 696/768 corpus vectors);
  negative strides; `--features unchecked`; the film-grain corpus group at
  t>1 (a pre-existing whole-plane double-&mut on main -- see the doc).
